tabulate-rust incorporates no upstream source code: it is an independent
Rust implementation of the table-formatting behavior described by the
upstream project below. The pure-Python fallback
(`tabulate/_pure.py`) is a byte-identical copy of the upstream 0.10.0
module, used when the Rust extension is unavailable or the input is
outside the kernel's exact domain (and as the correctness oracle for
the equivalence suite):

  astanin/python-tabulate — https://github.com/astanin/python-tabulate
  Copyright (c) 2011-2020 Sergey Astanin and contributors; MIT
  (see LICENSE, which is the upstream MIT text).

`tests/upstream/` are the upstream 0.10.0 test files, unmodified.
